.TH E2FSCK 1 "2026" "KERNEL32" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
e2fsck \- verifie un systeme de fichiers ext2/ext3/ext4 / check an ext2/ext3/ext4 file system
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B e2fsck
[-fnpvy] device
.br
.B fsck
[-t type] [-AN] [options] [device...]
.br
.SH DESCRIPTION
Read-only checker (every answer is "no", like e2fsck -n): superblock and group descriptors, pass 1 (inodes, blocks, sizes, i_blocks, blocks claimed twice), pass
2 (directories), pass 3 (connectivity), pass 4 (link counts), pass 5 (bitmaps and free counters). Output follows e2fsck. Exit status 0 when clean, 4 when errors
are left. Block maps and extents are understood; no repair is done. fsck runs fsck.TYPE according to -t or /etc/fstab.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -f
Force a full check even if the file system is marked clean.
.TP
.B -n
Read-only (always the case).
.SH SEE ALSO
mount(1)
